/T (A virtual function is a member function that is defined within a base class using the keyword virtual and is expected to be re-defined \(overridden\) in the derived class.)
/E (A virtual function is a member function that is defined within a base class using the keyword virtual and is expected to be re-defined \(overridden\) in the derived class.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
endobj
364 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 1215 0 R
/T (Virtual functions are used to vary the behavior of member functions of a base class in the derived class at runtime, thereby leading to runtime polymorphism.)
/E (Virtual functions are used to vary the behavior of member functions of a base class in the derived class at runtime, thereby leading to runtime polymorphism.)
/Pg 10 0 R
>>
endobj
